### 🔎 Observation

The quality classes are not evenly distributed.

Some quality scores contain significantly more observations than others. In particular, middle-quality wines are generally more common than extreme quality scores.

### ⚠️ Effect of Class Imbalance

Class imbalance can cause a model to favour majority classes.

For example, a model may achieve reasonable overall accuracy while performing poorly on rare quality classes.

Therefore, stratified splitting and class-wise evaluation using a classification report and confusion matrix are important.

